{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/ConsentDropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reports wait until they are read. A record dropped for room is reported as it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped; while that report waits unread, later ones merge into it, one report counting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them all across their timestamps. So the reports waiting unread hold at most one overflow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report between any two others (denials and finished trackers), however many events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overflow. The sequence has one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consumer, and ends once the consent is gone."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trackers\/consent\/dropreports"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent\/dropReports","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop of held or recovered records, in the order they happen."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"